<title>BRAZIL: Dry weather prevails in Brazil CS sugar areas.</title>
<headline>Dry weather prevails in Brazil CS sugar areas.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The weather is forecast to remain dry in Brazil's center-south sugar cane growing regions, creating good conditions for harvesting and loading sugar at ports, independent consultants DataNet-AgriCommodities said.</p>
<p>A cold front was set to arrive in the south on July 31 but was not seen bringing any rain to producing areas and ports in the center-south.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
